---
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { profilePageSchema } from '../lib/schema';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About MD Anik Hasan | Founder and Software Builder"
  description="MD Anik Hasan is a Computer Science and Engineering student at United International University who builds full-stack web products, custom software, and Boilabin."
  schema={profilePageSchema()}
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="About"
    title="Most of my time goes into building things that have to work."
    intro="I’m Anik, a Computer Science and Engineering student at United International University, the founder of Boilabin, and a full-stack web and software developer in Dhaka."
    workshop="Builder Profile"
  />

  <div class="content-layout">
    <aside class="content-rail" aria-label="Profile summary">
      <div>
        <p class="rail-label">Based in</p>
        <p>Dhaka, Bangladesh</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="rail-label">Studying</p>
        <p>Computer Science and Engineering at UIU</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="rail-label">Available for</p>
        <p>Full-stack web and custom software projects</p>
      </div>
    </aside>

    <article class="prose">
      <h2>Three things take up most of my time</h2>
      <p>
        Right now, my work falls into three buckets: running Boilabin, taking on web and software
        projects, and studying Computer Science and Engineering at United International University.
      </p>
      <p>
        Boilabin is the biggest one. I started it in Bangladesh and built the product from top to
        bottom: the storefront, backend, and the systems keeping accounts, listings, and orders
        moving. I’m still the person running it and improving it day to day.
      </p>
      <p>
        The rest of my work sits around that. I build full-stack websites and web applications, and
        I make custom desktop software or automation when a project needs something outside a
        browser entirely. SoctuKit, the UIU Discord Bot, and Salty Potato AI each show a different
        part of that work.
      </p>

      <h2>I do not stop at “technically works”</h2>
      <p>
        If an interaction feels clumsy or an edge case has been ignored, I keep working until the
        result feels right, not merely functional. That sometimes means I spend longer on the small
        details than expected. I have made my peace with that.
      </p>
      <p>
        I also care about the parts most people never see: loading behavior, failure states, local
        data, installation, deployment, and whether the product is still understandable six months
        after it ships.
      </p>

      <h2>Say hello</h2>
      <p>
        Outside the work, I’m easy to talk to. If you have a project in mind, or even just a useful
        technical question, reach out.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/hire/">Tell me about a project</a> or
        <a href="/contact/">choose a contact route</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
